WEBVTT

00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:04.980
Satoshi, who aims to battle
the Supreme Monarch, Dande...

00:00:05.370 --> 00:00:10.110
And Go, who dreams of catching every Pokémon
to work his way up to Mew...

00:00:10.110 --> 00:00:15.250
This is the story of their lives and adventures.

00:00:22.330 --> 00:00:25.440
Fossils are <i>enchanting!</i>

00:00:25.440 --> 00:00:29.500
The largest-ever Tatetops,
restored from a Fossil!

00:00:29.500 --> 00:00:33.630
All the good little kids,
come see this <i>enchanting</i> sight!

00:00:34.130 --> 00:00:36.310
The largest-ever...

00:00:36.310 --> 00:00:37.870
Tatetops...

00:00:37.870 --> 00:00:41.230
Awesome!
Let’s check it out, Go!

00:00:41.230 --> 00:00:44.230
Yeah, let’s!
To the Museum of Science!

00:00:44.230 --> 00:00:45.480
When are we going?
Right now?

00:00:45.480 --> 00:00:46.570
What should I do?

00:00:46.570 --> 00:00:47.230
Of course!
What should I do?

00:00:47.610 --> 00:00:50.100
Hmm?
Your personal research project?

00:00:50.100 --> 00:00:50.980
Yeah...

00:00:50.980 --> 00:00:54.360
How about researching Fossils?

00:00:54.360 --> 00:00:55.850
Fossils?

00:00:55.850 --> 00:00:58.350
You can join Satoshi and Go.

00:00:58.350 --> 00:00:59.200
Huh?

00:00:59.200 --> 00:01:00.780
All right!

00:01:00.780 --> 00:01:02.370
Let’s go, right now!

00:01:02.540 --> 00:01:03.710
See ya later!

00:01:03.710 --> 00:01:05.280
H-Hey!

00:01:05.280 --> 00:01:08.810
Enjoy the <i>enchanting</i>
mysteries of the ancient!

00:02:42.590 --> 00:02:48.020
The Fossil Pokémon!
A Miraculous Restoration,

00:02:48.020 --> 00:02:48.830
Museum of Science, Nibi City, Kanto Region

00:02:48.830 --> 00:02:51.980
This is the Museum of Science in Nibi City.
Museum of Science, Nibi City, Kanto Region

00:02:52.890 --> 00:02:56.640
Many people have come here to
observe the Fossil Pokémon Exhibition.

00:02:58.610 --> 00:03:00.360
A real live Omunite!

00:03:00.360 --> 00:03:03.170
Look, Pikachu! A Kabuto!

00:03:05.240 --> 00:03:07.740
Daddy, it’s a Kabutops!

00:03:07.740 --> 00:03:07.760
Look, Go, a Kabuto!

00:03:07.760 --> 00:03:09.910
Satoshi, it’s a real live Omunite!
Look, Go, a Kabuto!

00:03:09.910 --> 00:03:11.860
Whoa, an Omunite!
Whoa, a real Kabuto!

00:03:11.860 --> 00:03:15.130
Man, I wanna catch <i>all</i> the
Fossil Pokémon here!

00:03:15.130 --> 00:03:17.960
Wait... So where’s the Tatetops?

00:03:18.560 --> 00:03:20.630
Probably over there.

00:03:20.630 --> 00:03:27.140
The line for the largest-ever Tatetops exhibition
is closed for the day.

00:03:27.140 --> 00:03:28.520
No way!

00:03:28.520 --> 00:03:30.390
Closed?!

00:03:31.520 --> 00:03:33.390
I wanted to meet...

00:03:33.390 --> 00:03:35.020
...the real live Tatetops...

00:03:35.020 --> 00:03:36.940
Guess you just have to give up.

00:03:37.920 --> 00:03:40.650
But it looks like
they’re doing something over there.

00:03:41.400 --> 00:03:43.790
Fossil Excavation!

00:03:43.790 --> 00:03:47.730
Right now, you can keep one of your
excavated Fossils as a souvenir!

00:03:47.730 --> 00:03:51.130
If it’s in good condition, there’s a good chance
you can have it restored!

00:03:51.130 --> 00:03:53.630
Fossils are <i>enchanting!</i>

00:03:53.630 --> 00:03:54.810
You hear that?

00:03:54.810 --> 00:03:57.780
Does that mean a chance at
getting a Fossil Pokémon?!

00:03:57.780 --> 00:04:00.210
Sounds fun! Let’s do it!

00:04:00.210 --> 00:04:00.920
Yeah!

00:04:01.090 --> 00:04:03.160
We’re in!

00:04:03.160 --> 00:04:04.840
Hey...

00:04:15.990 --> 00:04:17.900
Look here!
I got something!

00:04:18.660 --> 00:04:21.970
Hmm... I don’t think
that’s a Pokémon Fossil.

00:04:22.640 --> 00:04:24.100
I’ve had it!

00:04:24.100 --> 00:04:28.660
Who was the <i>genius</i> that said
we could get loads of Fossil Pokémon here?!

00:04:28.660 --> 00:04:30.040
You, meow.

00:04:30.460 --> 00:04:31.410
It was you.

00:04:34.080 --> 00:04:37.180
Me? Well, then, who told <i>me?!</i>

00:04:37.180 --> 00:04:39.840
Whatever. I’ll just make
a Pokémon from stone.

00:04:39.840 --> 00:04:41.550
Don’t sulk.

00:04:42.180 --> 00:04:43.050
Sheesh...

00:04:43.050 --> 00:04:45.050
I got some kind of Fossil!

00:04:45.430 --> 00:04:47.180
<i>The brat boy?!</i>

00:04:47.180 --> 00:04:48.700
What kind of Fossil?

00:04:48.700 --> 00:04:50.160
<i>Some</i> kind of Fossil!

00:04:50.160 --> 00:04:51.810
Doesn’t look like a Pokémon.

00:04:51.810 --> 00:04:53.460
Is that even a Fossil?

00:04:53.460 --> 00:04:56.640
Fossils are <i>enchanting!</i>

00:04:56.640 --> 00:05:02.010
Fossils are records of history dating back
hundreds of thousands, even millions of years!

00:05:02.010 --> 00:05:04.950
They are filled with <i>enchantment!</i>

00:05:05.550 --> 00:05:06.600
Chief!

00:05:06.600 --> 00:05:08.410
We met in Isshu, right?

00:05:08.450 --> 00:05:12.700
<i>Enchanting</i>, isn’t it?

00:05:12.790 --> 00:05:17.630
No! I am the president
of the Museum of Science!

00:05:17.630 --> 00:05:19.800
Please, call me President!

00:05:19.800 --> 00:05:20.880
Twinkle!

00:05:21.330 --> 00:05:23.130
President...

00:05:23.130 --> 00:05:26.630
That’s the Fossil of
a Pokémon’s footprint!

00:05:26.630 --> 00:05:31.010
It proves that this Pokémon
walked this very ground long ago!

00:05:31.010 --> 00:05:34.640
Truly <i>enchanting!</i>

00:05:34.640 --> 00:05:36.740
It was a footprint?

00:05:36.740 --> 00:05:39.440
So, do you know what this is?

00:05:41.020 --> 00:05:42.240
A fang?

00:05:42.240 --> 00:05:43.950
Isn’t it a horn?

00:05:43.950 --> 00:05:45.650
Some kind of claw?

00:05:45.650 --> 00:05:50.240
Correct! This is a Claw Fossil,
from a Pokémon known as Anopth!

00:05:50.690 --> 00:05:52.240
From Anopth?

00:05:52.240 --> 00:06:00.470
Anopth is believed to have used its extending claws
to catch prey hiding among rocks on the seafloor.

00:06:00.470 --> 00:06:03.500
It is truly <i>enchanting!</i>

00:06:03.500 --> 00:06:05.400
<i>Cool...</i>

00:06:08.260 --> 00:06:15.140
Fossils are records that mark the locations
where long-gone Pokémon once lived.

00:06:15.140 --> 00:06:17.540
So they’re like a natural
Pokémon Index?

00:06:17.540 --> 00:06:18.900
Exactly!

00:06:18.900 --> 00:06:26.810
With a Fossil as pristine as this one, it might be possible
to restore it to its old self using the restoration device.

00:06:26.810 --> 00:06:30.530
Well? Do you understand
how <i>enchanting</i> Fossils are now?

00:06:30.530 --> 00:06:31.990
Yeah!

00:06:31.990 --> 00:06:35.620
All right! I’m gonna get my own
Fossil Pokémon, for sure!

00:06:35.620 --> 00:06:36.800
Me, too!

00:06:38.000 --> 00:06:40.670
I guess I’ll try searching, too.

00:06:40.670 --> 00:06:44.050
If you find anything,
bring it to the restoration room.

00:06:44.050 --> 00:06:45.840
I’ll evaluate it for you.

00:06:45.840 --> 00:06:47.530
<i>Got it!</i>

00:06:47.530 --> 00:06:48.440
You hear that?

00:06:48.440 --> 00:06:50.960
Sure did. Let’s drop
the search for Fossils...

00:06:50.960 --> 00:06:54.180
...and nab the restored
Fossil Pokémon instead, meow!

00:06:54.180 --> 00:06:56.750
Then Sakaki will be delighted!

00:07:04.570 --> 00:07:07.440
Looks like there’s
something in here!

00:07:07.440 --> 00:07:08.510
Pikachu.

00:07:09.280 --> 00:07:12.110
Iron Tail!

00:07:20.670 --> 00:07:23.960
Let’s do this, Golugh! Go!

00:07:27.570 --> 00:07:30.630
Golugh! Let’s search for Fossils!

00:07:48.530 --> 00:07:50.240
Huh? What’s up?

00:07:50.240 --> 00:07:51.360
What could this be?

00:07:52.650 --> 00:07:55.170
The shape looks like a Shellder...

00:07:55.170 --> 00:07:57.410
But it might not be...

00:07:57.830 --> 00:07:59.200
Could it be
a brand new discovery?!

00:07:59.200 --> 00:08:02.550
Go, what do you think...?

00:08:09.260 --> 00:08:10.630
All right...

00:08:10.630 --> 00:08:13.310
I’ll get the President
to look at this.

00:08:13.310 --> 00:08:15.160
I’m coming with you.

00:08:15.160 --> 00:08:16.210
Thanks.

00:08:34.770 --> 00:08:37.160
Go, time’s up.

00:08:41.410 --> 00:08:44.440
Huh? When did...?

00:08:46.970 --> 00:08:48.670
Hey, Go!

00:08:49.880 --> 00:08:51.400
Sheesh...

00:08:51.400 --> 00:08:54.350
Too bad it wasn’t a new discovery.

00:08:55.250 --> 00:08:58.460
Yeah. But I’ve got plenty of material
for my research project.

00:08:58.460 --> 00:09:02.140
What’s this?!

00:09:10.650 --> 00:09:12.790
This is no Fossil.

00:09:15.430 --> 00:09:18.070
It is something even more incredible!

00:09:19.750 --> 00:09:24.750
This is Amber. Ancient tree resin
that has hardened and turned to stone.

00:09:24.750 --> 00:09:28.920
And not just any Amber,
it’s Secret Amber!

00:09:28.920 --> 00:09:31.050
Secret Amber?

00:09:31.050 --> 00:09:33.750
Indeed. Unlike regular Amber,

00:09:33.750 --> 00:09:37.930
it holds the genes of
a Pokémon from its era within.

00:09:37.930 --> 00:09:39.430
Genes?

00:09:39.430 --> 00:09:43.030
You could call them
the blueprints of life.

00:09:43.030 --> 00:09:47.050
We can restore old Pokémon with far more accuracy
from these than we can with Fossils!

00:09:47.050 --> 00:09:49.520
That’s awesome!
Let’s give it a shot!

00:09:49.520 --> 00:09:50.670
Please do.

00:09:50.670 --> 00:09:53.230
Leave the <i>enchantment</i> to me!

00:09:53.230 --> 00:09:54.150
All right!

00:10:03.240 --> 00:10:04.880
That should do it.

00:10:04.880 --> 00:10:07.410
Now we just have to
wait until tomorrow morning.

00:10:07.410 --> 00:10:09.160
Tomorrow, huh?

00:10:09.160 --> 00:10:12.470
Then let’s all spend the night
at the Pokémon Center.

00:10:29.950 --> 00:10:32.670
What Fossil Pokémon
do you think we’ll get?

00:10:34.990 --> 00:10:37.930
Maybe an Omustar?
Or Kabutops?

00:10:37.930 --> 00:10:39.950
Or maybe something
even greater!

00:10:40.850 --> 00:10:44.260
I can’t wait for tomorrow!

00:10:46.580 --> 00:10:48.170
Pocket Monsters!

00:10:52.630 --> 00:10:57.550
Kabutops

00:10:57.980 --> 00:11:00.550
It’s going smoothly.

00:11:00.550 --> 00:11:03.800
I’m sure we’ll find a happy,
healthy Pokémon here tomorrow.

00:11:04.170 --> 00:11:08.690
Truly <i>enchanting!</i>

00:11:09.480 --> 00:11:12.350
Mister <i>Enchanting</i> finally left.

00:11:12.350 --> 00:11:14.900
It’s been so long since we snuck in.

00:11:14.900 --> 00:11:17.990
I feel totally stiff
from hiding so long, meow.

00:11:23.280 --> 00:11:25.390
He said it’d be done
in the morning, yeah?

00:11:26.740 --> 00:11:27.980
That’s quite the wait.

00:11:27.980 --> 00:11:29.860
But we just gotta be patient, meow.

00:11:32.320 --> 00:11:35.820
I can’t wait
all the way till morning!

00:11:37.530 --> 00:11:40.740
So this dial controls it...

00:11:45.760 --> 00:11:46.640
Bingo!

00:11:46.640 --> 00:11:47.720
Perfect, meow!

00:11:47.720 --> 00:11:49.310
Well done!

00:11:49.310 --> 00:11:53.090
A simple restoration device
is no problem for the mighty Kojiro...

00:11:54.070 --> 00:11:55.360
Isn’t this, like, kinda bad?

00:12:01.650 --> 00:12:03.210
W-What?

00:12:04.900 --> 00:12:06.120
Hey!

00:12:06.830 --> 00:12:08.240
What was that sound?

00:12:08.940 --> 00:12:10.050
I don’t know.

00:12:10.820 --> 00:12:15.040
But that smoke seems to be coming
from the Museum of Science!

00:12:18.360 --> 00:12:20.030
President!

00:12:20.030 --> 00:12:20.800
It’s you three!

00:12:20.800 --> 00:12:22.950
What happened?

00:12:22.950 --> 00:12:25.020
The restoration device
was destroyed!

00:12:25.020 --> 00:12:29.310
What? Oh, no!
What about my Fossil Pokémon?!

00:12:31.680 --> 00:12:33.850
It’s already restored.

00:12:33.850 --> 00:12:38.150
But this is strange...
It shouldn’t be ready yet.

00:12:41.320 --> 00:12:42.990
Go, there’s something
over there!

00:12:44.410 --> 00:12:45.350
Go!

00:12:51.950 --> 00:12:53.750
Where are you headed, Go?!

00:12:53.750 --> 00:12:56.300
That’s my Pokémon!

00:12:57.540 --> 00:13:00.000
I’m coming, too! Pikachu!

00:13:02.030 --> 00:13:03.210
Wait!

00:13:07.140 --> 00:13:08.370
Over there?

00:13:15.980 --> 00:13:17.600
Where are you?

00:13:19.050 --> 00:13:20.340
Hey!

00:13:20.340 --> 00:13:22.440
Go!

00:13:26.310 --> 00:13:27.210
What’s up?

00:13:29.420 --> 00:13:30.640
There’s something there.

00:13:31.270 --> 00:13:32.900
Stand back, Koharu.

00:13:32.900 --> 00:13:34.540
Oh... Okay.

00:13:42.270 --> 00:13:43.090
Greetings.

00:13:44.290 --> 00:13:45.220
It’s you guys!

00:13:47.280 --> 00:13:49.600
If you say “It’s you guys!”...

00:13:50.070 --> 00:13:52.850
We’ll answer out of
sympathy for the world!

00:13:54.180 --> 00:13:56.580
To protect the world from devastation.

00:13:56.580 --> 00:13:59.520
To preserve world peace.

00:14:00.060 --> 00:14:02.980
Championing the evils
of truth and love.

00:14:02.980 --> 00:14:05.740
We’re the lovely, charming villains.

00:14:06.320 --> 00:14:07.090
Musashi!

00:14:07.090 --> 00:14:08.200
Kojiro!

00:14:08.200 --> 00:14:12.040
The Team Rocket duo
soars through the galaxy!

00:14:12.040 --> 00:14:15.080
Like a white hole,
a white tomorrow awaits us!

00:14:15.080 --> 00:14:17.400
Just kidding, meow!

00:14:21.540 --> 00:14:23.000
Team Rocket!

00:14:23.000 --> 00:14:25.170
So you were the ones
who destroyed the device?!

00:14:25.170 --> 00:14:29.860
We were planning to offer up
some Fossil Pokémon to Sakaki...

00:14:29.860 --> 00:14:33.790
But then the machine up and exploded!
What a piece of junk!

00:14:33.790 --> 00:14:37.120
But if we just nab Pikachu instead,
there’s no problem!

00:14:37.120 --> 00:14:38.890
Vending, come on!

00:14:55.860 --> 00:14:59.480
Rocket Vending Secret!

00:15:07.340 --> 00:15:09.680
I wonder, what’ll I get?

00:15:14.300 --> 00:15:17.310
The Poison Needle Pokémon,
Nidorino!

00:15:18.310 --> 00:15:21.310
The Rock Pokémon, Gorone!

00:15:23.060 --> 00:15:25.360
Koharu, find Go!

00:15:25.360 --> 00:15:27.310
I’ll deal with these guys!

00:15:27.310 --> 00:15:28.130
Okay!

00:15:28.990 --> 00:15:30.290
Let’s do this, Pikachu!

00:15:31.320 --> 00:15:33.450
Nidorino! Venom Shock!

00:15:33.450 --> 00:15:35.030
Gorone! Rollout!

00:15:38.540 --> 00:15:40.710
Pikachu! 100,000 Volts!

00:15:45.630 --> 00:15:47.630
Was that...?

00:15:55.420 --> 00:15:57.470
Rotom, who’s that Pokémon?

00:15:58.140 --> 00:16:02.190
Ptera! Fossil Pokémon!
Rock/Flying type!

00:16:02.190 --> 00:16:05.640
A widely accepted theory is that it went extinct
due to a large meteor impact!

00:16:05.640 --> 00:16:08.010
In ancient times,
it ruled the skies!

00:16:12.370 --> 00:16:16.780
Ruled the skies...
That’s so cool!

00:16:16.780 --> 00:16:19.880
Ptera, listen to me!

00:16:25.460 --> 00:16:28.260
Rabbifoot, use Double Kick!

00:16:30.260 --> 00:16:31.850
Rabbifoot!

00:16:35.890 --> 00:16:38.080
Are you okay?! Come back!

00:16:39.530 --> 00:16:43.060
In that case...
Golugh, go!

00:16:57.170 --> 00:16:58.250
Guard yourself!

00:17:02.150 --> 00:17:04.010
We’re gonna stop it from moving!

00:17:04.010 --> 00:17:05.420
Luster Cannon!

00:17:13.760 --> 00:17:15.780
Another Luster Cannon!

00:17:28.400 --> 00:17:29.690
Golugh!

00:17:32.650 --> 00:17:34.310
Guard!

00:17:36.950 --> 00:17:40.660
Ptera used to rule the skies...?
I can believe it!

00:17:41.780 --> 00:17:46.710
But that’s all the more reason
to win and make it my partner!

00:17:46.710 --> 00:17:48.180
Go!

00:17:48.710 --> 00:17:50.210
Satoshi’s in trouble!

00:17:50.210 --> 00:17:51.260
Satoshi?

00:17:51.260 --> 00:17:55.570
It was Team Rocket who destroyed the device!
Satoshi is battling them right now!

00:17:58.250 --> 00:17:59.970
I’ve got my hands full, too!

00:18:02.350 --> 00:18:04.250
Nidorino! Poison Needle!

00:18:05.450 --> 00:18:06.730
Fall back, Pikachu!

00:18:09.160 --> 00:18:11.250
Don’t let him escape!
Use Tackle!

00:18:14.940 --> 00:18:17.530
Pikachu!
Use Electroweb on those trees!

00:18:21.870 --> 00:18:24.750
He blocked his own path, meow!

00:18:26.370 --> 00:18:28.750
Now slip through the web!

00:18:42.640 --> 00:18:45.840
<i>What an awful feeling!</i>

00:18:50.300 --> 00:18:52.140
You did it, Pikachu!

00:18:58.830 --> 00:19:00.010
How is Golugh?!

00:19:00.010 --> 00:19:01.410
It’s fine!

00:19:07.660 --> 00:19:10.310
I figured it would use Iron Head.

00:19:10.310 --> 00:19:12.920
Golugh, hit it back
with an Arm Hammer!

00:19:17.510 --> 00:19:18.670
Luster Cannon!

00:19:31.820 --> 00:19:33.190
Go!

00:19:44.910 --> 00:19:47.270
Go, don’t!
It’s dangerous!

00:19:50.310 --> 00:19:52.960
You were scared, yeah?

00:19:53.550 --> 00:19:56.260
You woke up in a world
you didn’t know...

00:19:58.250 --> 00:20:02.260
But this era isn’t all bad.

00:20:05.760 --> 00:20:10.270
You should take your time
and get used to it, together with me.

00:20:26.400 --> 00:20:27.970
All right...

00:20:27.970 --> 00:20:30.370
Monster Ball, go!

00:20:43.530 --> 00:20:46.880
Ptera’s data will be
added to the Index!

00:20:51.430 --> 00:20:53.090
You got it?

00:20:53.760 --> 00:20:56.560
Yeah! It’s my new partner!

00:20:57.040 --> 00:21:00.270
Ptera, go!

00:21:04.280 --> 00:21:06.700
Happy to have you, Ptera!

00:21:10.450 --> 00:21:12.540
Whoa, it’s a Ptera!

00:21:20.820 --> 00:21:23.150
I see... So that’s how you caught it!

00:21:23.150 --> 00:21:25.690
Yeah! I had so much fun!

00:21:25.690 --> 00:21:26.650
Me, too!

00:21:26.650 --> 00:21:27.800
Same!

00:21:30.130 --> 00:21:34.530
Go caught Ptera,
which was restored from the Secret Amber.

00:21:34.530 --> 00:21:38.870
Satoshi and Koharu have grown a bit
through their encounter with Fossil Pokémon.

00:21:38.870 --> 00:21:42.550
Next time, let’s go to
another new adventure!

00:21:51.040 --> 00:21:51.810
Mew!

00:21:51.810 --> 00:21:52.560
Warrgle!

00:21:52.560 --> 00:21:53.350
Runpappa!

